--- IR --->
# the three placements the module system is built on, read off one dump.
#
# `tripled` is `#[inline]` and `Box<int32>::get` is a generic instantiation, so both are ODR-shared: the
# body is emitted into every unit that references it, under linkonce_odr, exactly as C++ treats an
# implicitly-instantiated template. `doubled` is neither, so it stays a single external definition owned by
# the unit of the module that declares it.
#
# this is the invariant an object cache rests on. A module's emitted code has to be a function of its own
# source, and it stops being one the moment a consumer can cause a definition to appear in the *library's*
# unit - which is what happened before instances were placed this way.
CHECK: define linkonce_odr i32 @_modcore_tripledZZMLPi
CHECK: define linkonce_odr %"Box<int32>" @_modcore_BoxZZMLPiGMLPi
CHECK: define linkonce_odr i32 @_modcore_MN7modcore3BoxE_get
CHECK: define i32 @_modcore_doubledZZMLPi
